/**
 * PANCREATIC CANCER: LIVING WITH IT, CARE AND DECISIONS (UK and NHS focus). Facts checked 2026-09-24.
 *
 * The patient side of the pancreatic cancer record, to the gallbladder and TNBC standard (./gallbladder-living.ts,
 * ./tnbc-living.ts): ten decision rows the decisions page turns into sections (surgery first or chemotherapy first when
 * the tumour is resectable or borderline; which chemotherapy by fitness; chemotherapy after a Whipple operation; germline
 * testing and what BRCA means for olaparib and for the family; a stent or surgery for jaundice; pain including a coeliac
 * plexus block; pancreatic enzymes and diabetes; feeding and weight; a trial or standard treatment; palliative care early),
 * the hand-written question set the appointment sheet, prep pack and decision pages read (exported as
 * `pancreaticQuestions`, wired in src/data/questions.ts), and living-with material attached as sourced notes and links
 * to the side-effect and procedure records other files own (enzymes and weight loss, jaundice and itch, stents and
 * cholangitis, pain, fatigue, neuropathy, diarrhoea, neutropenia, blood clots, eating after surgery, emotional impact,
 * work and money, carers).
 *
 * This file creates no glossary terms: the glossary pass (agent A) owns them. Drafts for the terms this material wants
 * are exported as `pancreaticLivingTermDrafts`, written to the glossary standard so they can be registered by spreading
 * the array; the ids they use are referenced nowhere in the graph until then. Trials are owned by the registry pass
 * (agent B): rows here reference only trials already on the record (PRODIGE 24, PREOPANC, NAPOLI 3, POLO, ESPAC-5).
 *
 * Every medical statement points at an NHS, Pancreatic Cancer UK, Macmillan, Cancer Research UK, Maggie's or Marie Curie
 * page, NICE NG85 or a NICE appraisal, or a paper read through Europe PMC. Nothing here is advice; the pages say so the
 * way the site's other living-with material does. UK spelling, plain English, no em-dashes.
 *
 * The cancer record itself (`pancreatic`) lives in src/data/cancers.ts with the treatment rows in ./pancreatic.ts; if it
 * is renamed, change PANCREATIC_CANCER_ID and the questions key together. The checklist for the first 60 days is in
 * src/data/first-60-days-checklists.ts, the red cards in src/data/red-flags.ts (cancerIds: ["pancreatic"]) and the
 * decision aid in src/data/decision-tools/pancreatic-first-treatment.ts.
 */
